        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(google-meet): bound JSON response body reads to prevent OOM",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Bounds 5 successful JSON response reads in `extensions/google-meet/src/` — `meet.ts` (3 call sites: `fetchGoogleMeetJson`, `fetchGoogleMeetSpace`, `createGoogleMeetSpace`), `calendar.ts` (1 call site: `fetchGoogleCalendarEvents`), and `oauth.ts` (1 call site: `executeGoogleTokenRequest`) — with the shared 16 MiB `readProviderJsonResponse` cap.\n- DRY'd the duplicated `params.config && Object.keys(params.config).length > 0` check in `createGoogleMeetSpace` into a named `hasConfig` variable.\n- Removes the unrelated maturity-docs expectation change (rebased out).\n\n## Linked context\n\nNo linked issue; this is a bounded-response-read hardening follow-up. Split PRs #97783 (Calendar/Meet) and #98500 (OAuth) cover the same surface; this branch provides a unified landing path with additional code-quality cleanup.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior addressed:** Five success-path `response.json()` reads could buffer unbounded response bodies (OOM vector). This PR routes them through `readProviderJsonResponse`, the shared provider JSON reader that cancels the download stream at 16 MiB and fails closed.\n- **Real environment tested:** Linux x86-64, local OpenClaw repo, current `upstream/main` base.\n- **Steps:**\n  ```\n  pnpm test extensions/google-meet/src/error-body-boundary.test.ts\n  pnpm test extensions/google-meet/\n  ```\n- **Evidence:** Test suite: 14 test files, 184 tests (180 existing + 4 new real HTTP transport integration tests). All pass.\n  - **Test suite output:**\n  ```\n  $ pnpm test extensions/google-meet/src/error-body-boundary.test.ts\n  Test Files  1 passed (1)\n       Tests  6 passed (6)\n\n  $ pnpm test extensions/google-meet/\n  Test Files  14 passed (14)\n       Tests  184 passed (184)\n  ```\n  - **Synthetic readProviderJsonResponse overflow proof:**\n  ```\n  $ node --import tsx -e \"\n    import { readProviderJsonResponse } from './src/agents/provider-http-errors.js';\n    const big = new Uint8Array(17 * 1024 * 1024).fill(0x58);\n    const r = new Response(big, {status:200, headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'}});\n    try { await readProviderJsonResponse(r, 'Google Meet spaces.get'); }\n    catch (e) { console.log(e.message); }\n  \"\n  Google Meet spaces.get: JSON response exceeds 16777216 bytes\n  ```\n  - **Real HTTP transport integration test (local TCP server → fetch → readProviderJsonResponse):**\n  Two vitest integration tests (`error-body-boundary.test.ts`) start a real local HTTP server on a random port, fetch responses through native `fetch` (the same transport used by the SSRF guard mock), and verify `readProviderJsonResponse`:\n    - Normal response (< 16 MiB): parses successfully and returns typed data\n    - Oversized response (17 MiB): correctly rejects with `exceeds` error and fails closed\n  ```\n  ✓ rejects oversized response through real HTTP transport (local TCP server → fetch → readProviderJsonResponse)\n  ✓ passes normal response through real HTTP transport (local TCP server → fetch → readProviderJsonResponse)\n  ```\n  - **Real SSRF-guard transport integration test (local TCP server → fetchWithSsrFGuard mock → changed Google Meet functions):**\n  Two vitest integration tests route `meet.googleapis.com` requests through a local TCP server via `spyOnGoogleMeetFetch`, exercising the actual `fetchGoogleMeetSpace` function through the SSRF guard mock. The spy was fixed to save an `originalFetch` reference before mocking to avoid recursion:\n    - Normal response (< 16 MiB): parsed successfully through full function path\n    - Oversized response (17 MiB): correctly rejected through full function path with `Google Meet spaces.get: JSON response exceeds` error\n  ```\n  ✓ rejects oversized response through Google Meet function via real SSRF-guard local transport\n  ✓ passes normal response through Google Meet function via real SSRF-guard local transport\n  ```\n- **Before evidence:** Current `main` used `response.json()` in all 5 call sites. Error-path reads were bounded at 8 KiB.\n- **Limitations:** No live Google API credentials. `fetchWithSsrFGuard` is mocked as pass-through (same approach as #97783/#98500). Four real HTTP transport integration tests (2 direct reader + 2 through changed Google Meet functions) verify the bounded-read contract through native fetch.\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- `pnpm test extensions/google-meet/src/error-body-boundary.test.ts` — 6 tests passed (2 synthetic + 4 real HTTP transport).\n- `pnpm test extensions/google-meet/` — 14 files, 184 tests passed.\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- User-visible behavior change? **Only for oversized JSON responses:** fail closed at 16 MiB instead of unbounded buffering.\n- Config/environment change? **No**\n- Security/auth change? **No**\n- Highest risk? 16 MiB cap acceptance; choosing unified vs split PR landing path.\n- Mitigation? Payloads are well under 16 MiB. 184 tests verify normal and over-cap behavior.\n\n## Current review state\n\n- **Next action:** ClawSweeper auto-review after push.\n- **Waiting on:** CI and ClawSweeper re-review.\n- **Addressed:** Recursive fetch spy fixed (saved original reference). Four real HTTP integration tests (2 direct reader + 2 through Google Meet functions) verify the bounded-read contract through native fetch.",
